From: hanson@hss.caltech.edu (Robin Hanson)
Date: Fri, 16 Sep 1994 10:45:05 -0700
Subject: [#94-9-179] What Happens First?

In general, I think the most interesting question to ask about the future is
which of the many envisioned big future changes is most likely to happen
first.  While we might have some hope of projecting the consequences of the
first or maybe even the second big change, it's hard to see much point in
projecting beyond that.  Here are some big envisioned changes to
consider.  Feel free to add more.

Big Fraction of Economy Off Earth
Big Fraction of Economy out of Solar System
Really Cheap Fusion Power
Nukes as Cheap as Tanks
Nukes as Cheap as Handguns
ICBMs as Cheap as Tanks
Two Century Meat Lifespans
Indefinite Meat Lifespans
Uploads
Uploads running 1000x Faster than Humans
Human-Brain Equivalent Computers on a Desk
Human-Level A.I.
Nanotech Factories
Reproducing Nanotech Assemblers
Reproducing Asteriod Eaters
Reproducing Starships
Most Publications are Electronic
Most Intellectual Publications are on Web
Big Fraction of Labor Telecommutes
Big Fraction of Economy Via CryptoNet and so UnGoverned 
Most Education Privatized
Most Law Enforcement Privatized
Most Law Choice Privatized
National Defense Privatized
Betting Markets a Big Policy Influence
Big Fraction of Research Funded Via Info and Other Prizes

So folks, what do you think will happen first, or waht before what else?

My opinion is that uploads come before human level AI, space
colonization, long meat lifespans, or reproducing nanotech assemblers.

Robin Hanson

